				<h2>3. Working with clients through iDAL</h2>
				
				<h3>How do I see the clients on the platform?</h3>
				<p>You can only see clients’ profiles on the platform after they option you for a project.</p>
				
				<h3>Who can see my profile at iDAL website? </h3>
				<p>Only iDAL and iDAL’s clients can see your profile.</p>
				
				<h3>Who are the clients on the iDAL platform?</h3>
				<p>Only those companies and creatives that work in fashion or marketing/advertising businesses are accepted to iDAL. We verify client’s corporate information and their IDs in order to ensure only relevant companies and brands contact you for projects.</p> 
				
				<h3>How can clients discover me on the platform?</h3>
{*				<p>It is only after you have been verified you can be visible to verified clients on the platform. On the calendar in your profile , you can decide if and when you want to be available for bookings or not. Your details and profile photographs are not available to unregistered or unverified visitors to the website, nor are they made publicly available without your written permission.</p>*}
				<p>In order to book a model, clients create a project where the list of applicable models for that job will appear in a search. They will list their proposed fee, date, location and type of job. You will not appear in searches of fees that are lower than your minimum fee, dates that you are not available or types of work that you do not wish to do.</p>

				<h3>How do I communicate with a client?</h3>
				<p>At iDAL the communication between you and a client happens in  pre-written wording. It means, after a client optioned you for a project, you will receive a message with all necessary details about the client and the project, such as name of the brand you will work for, location, date, time, things you need to have for a project and what you will be asked to do. You will also be proposed a day/hourly rate, which you may accept or negotiate.</p> 
				
				<h3>What do I do when the project is completed?</h3>
{*				<p>Please mark the job as ‘completed’ and leave a review to the client, to let us and future requested models know how it was. No further action is required. With iDAL, the payment will automatically be deposited into your account shortly. Don't forget to share your experience with your friends on Instagram with #iDALModel #iDALCommunity #iDALTalent</p>*}
				<p>After your job, please mark the job as ‘completed’ and leave a review for the client for our feedback. Your payment for the job will be automatically deposited into your bank account shortly. Feel free to share your experience on Instagram with #iDALModel #iDALCommunity #iDALTalent.</p>
				
				<h3>How does the rating system work?</h3>
{*				<p>The rating system allows a client and a model leave a review for each other’s performance. This helps making the industry more transparent, and in the long term helps to recognise issues. It also helps the iDAL community identifying the best performing talent as well as spotting unprofessional users. Models can leave public or anonymous reviews for clients after they have completed a project with them via iDAL. These reviews are made available to other models after they have been requested for a project by that client.</p>*}
				<p>The rating system allows models and clients to leave reviews for each other’s performance after a job, which helps to build transparency and flag any potential problems. The review process shows us who is performing well and who is in need of extra support from us. Models can leave public or anonymous reviews for clients, that will be published or directly sent to the client after they have worked with them via iDAL. This allows both client and model to continually better themselves and build an honest, supportive relationship. Reviews are available to other models to view after they have been optioned for a project by that client. </p>
				
				<h3>What if there is a dispute with the client?</h3>
				<p>If anything goes wrong, please contact us at support@idal.co. We will work directly with all of the parties to resolve the dispute. In extreme cases, if we believe that a client misrepresented a booking, we will serve as your advocate to ensure that the usage conforms to what was agreed between you and the client and our Terms and Conditions.</p>
				
				
				<h2>4. Cancellations </h2>
				
				<h3>What do I do if a client cancels last minute?</h3>
				<p>We are sorry for such occasions. But as you are aware, it can happen . Although we and the clients at iDAL always aim to organise everything upfront, some occasional cancellations may occur. If it happens, we will immediately notify you via email and through notification at iDAL website. Please check for updates before going to the location of your booking.</p>
				
				<h3>Can I cancel a job?</h3>
				<p>A client has made a lot of commitments in order to create a project, and they expect you to attend. We strongly recommend that you do not cancel your bookings unless you know you are absolutely unable to attend. In this case please cancel at least 24 hours before the project starts. Cancelling jobs can lower your rating, which could prevent you from booking great jobs  in the future.</p> 
				
				<h3>What if I need to cancel last minute?</h3>
{*				<p>If you need to cancel less than 24 hours before job starts, you need a legitimate reason for cancellation, such as proof from a doctor if you are ill. No-shows without explanation can lead to significant negative effects of your rating.</p> *}
				<p>If you urgently cannot attend a job, such as due to sickness or an emergency, please contact us as soon as possible and/or the client. No-shows without explanation will lead to effects in your rating and may result in you being asked to leave iDAL. </p>

				<h3>5. Payments</h3>
				
				<h3>What are the project rates?</h3>
{*				<p>Job postings have hourly or daily rates. At the moment a client can propose you any rate and you can accept or reject, or propose a different rate. We are currently developing a price-generation algorithm which will generate a price based on your own requirements, type of a project, usage of produced photographs or video footage, your rating etc. We will send you a notification when it’s ready.</p>*}
				<p>Job postings have hourly or daily rates which you are able to accept, reject or negotiate. If your minimum fee is very high, you will not appear in searches for jobs that are paid lower than this fee. </p>

				<h3>How do I get paid?</h3>
				<p>To receive payment, simply add your bank account number and your bank sort code. This information is securely stored by Stripe, our payment processing partner. Once your information has been entered, you can then get paid for the projects after they are completed.</p> 
				
				<h3>When will I get paid?</h3>
				<p>iDAL allows you to get paid as quickly as the day after your shoot. However, the payments can be delayed to a maximum of 30 days, depending on a client’s profile. If this is the case, you will be notified before you accept the booking offer.</p> 
				
				<h3>How can I view my payments status?</h3>
				<p>Under the ‘invoices’ page, you will find a summary of your payments.</p>  
				
				<h3>What commission does iDAL charge?</h3>
				<p>iDAL charges 10% fee from each booking that you complete. For example, if your agreed rate for a project is £1,000, you will receive £900.</p> 
				
				<h3>How secure is iDAL payment service?</h3>
				<p>iDAL uses Stripe for all payments. For more information, please visit <a href="https://stripe.com">the Stripe website</a>.</p>
				
				<h1>Information for creators</h1>
				
				<h2>1. Discovering and booking models at iDAL</h2>
				
				<h3>Who are the models? </h3>
{*				<p>We have a network of professional models that is constantly growing with both established models and new faces. We verify professional experience, social media presence and a look of each model to make sure you discover only a professional talent.</p>*}
				<p>Our models represent a diverse, high quality standard of talent. They are all verified by our Model Managers to ensure they are professional, with checks on experience, social media and personality. We personally ensure that each model is fully equipped with all of the knowledge and experience they need to deliver excellent service to you as a client. </p>
				
				<h3>How do I find a model at iDAL?</h3>
{*				<p>Verified users can find models at ‘Find a model’ page. Use our filters to discover models that fit your project best. Specify basic criteria such as height, dress size, location, skin or eye colour etc. If important to you - choose a minimum number of Instagram followers. Additionally, when you create a project you will be able to choose only those models who can work on your specified date and at your offered rate.</p>*}
				<p>In order to view iDAL models, create a Project (job posting). By using our filters, you can specify exactly what kind of model you would like to view - such as hair colour, eye colour, height, location, skin - even Instagram followers. Only models that fit your specified criteria will appear in the search, so if your proposed rate is too low models with higher rates may not appear. Models set their own minimum rates on iDAL. The models that appear in your search will be able to work on your specified date at your offered rate. </p>

				<h3>How do I book a model?</h3>
				<p>After you have created a project and found the models, simply click ‘option for project’ at a model’s profile page, select a project and a rate. You will be notified via both the platform and by email if a model accepts or rejects a booking.</p>
				
				<h3>How do I communicate with a model?</h3>
				<p>On the iDAL platform, communication between you and a model happens via pre-written wording, and no direct messages. It means, if you would like to book a model for a project, you need to create a project, fill all necessary details, and propose an hourly or daily rate. A model will receive a job offer with these details. If she accepts the offer, you will be immediately notified by email.</p>
				
				<h3>How do I send a model his or her call sheet?</h3>
				<p>Once your booking has been confirmed, you will be able to upload a call sheet under the ‘Projects’ page. The call sheet can be changed at any time before the start of a booking and the booked model receives a notification if you do so.</p>
				
				<h3>What are the rates for iDAL bookings?</h3>
				<p>When you create a project, you have an option to specify either a day or an hourly rate. This rate can be negotiated between you and a model. If a model does not accept your offered rate, she may offer you an alternative rate, and you have an option to accept it, negotiate back or decline a booking.</p> 
				
				<h3>Who can see my profile?</h3>
				<p>Only models that you have optioned or booked for your projects at iDAL can see your profile at iDAL. Other businesses cannot see your profile.</p>
				
				<h2>2. Cancellations and disputes</h2>
				
				<h3>What do I do if the model does not show up?</h3>
