				<p>In the unexpected event of a model not showing up, please contact us immediately. If a model is unable to attend the booking due to sickness, they will have to offer a Doctor’s note. In case of other emergency, we will liaise with you directly on the best way to resolve this issue.</p> 

				<p>No-shows are taken very seriously by iDAL, and if there is not a legitimate reason for this then please be assured that we will take appropriate action against the model and fully refund you, in addition to waiving our fees for your next booking.</p> 
				
				<h3>What do I do if a model cancels?</h3>
				<p>If a model cancels more than 24 hours before the project, you will be offered to replace her with your previously optioned models; if neither of them are available we will do our best replace her with a similar option.</p> 
				
				<h3>What do I do if a model cancels last minute?</h3>
{*				<p>If a model cancels a booking less than 24 hours before the project starts, we will do our best to replace her with your ‘options’. If none of the previously optioned models are available, you will be offered other similar iDAL models who are available last minute.</p> *}
				<p>If a model cancels within 24 hours, we will refund you 50% of your fee. Last minute cancellations are taken very seriously and we will take appropriate action against the model for this.  We will do our best to replace the model with another model that is appropriate for the job. </p>

				<h3>What if there is a dispute with a model?</h3>
				<p>If you have a dispute with a model that you have booked for a project at iDAL, please email us at support@idal.co. We will aim to resolve the issue as quickly as possible. Under extreme circumstances where a model fails to perform the services contracted in your agreement, a partial or full refund may be possible.</p>
				
				<h2>3. Creating and editing your projects</h2>
				
				<h3>How do I create a project?</h3>
				<p>Once your profile on iDAL is verified, you'll be able to create projects under the Projects page. Click on the Create a project button on left panel or under the Projects page on the left, and fill in all the necessary details.</p> 
				
				<h3>How do I edit or cancel a project? </h3>
				<p>After you have created a project, you will be able to make any necessary edits until your optioned models have accepted the booking request, or until you have finalised the project. Should you have to cancel a job, please note that doing so with less than 48 hours in advance will lower your rating, which may cause less models to be willing to accept your bookings in the future.</p> 
				
				<h3>How do I cancel a booking within 24 hours?</h3>
				<p>If you cancel a booking within 24 hours, the confirmed model is entitled to 50% of the fee. Please see our contract for this term. </p>
				
				<h3>What happens if I ‘finalise’ a project?</h3>
				<p>Once you finalise all project details and click ‘finalise’, the project details are considered accepted by yourself and all the models who have accepted the booking request. At this point the project cannot be edited. An invoice will be automatically generated and made available for settlement in the invoices page.</p>
				
				<h2>4. Payments</h2>
				<h3>What are the available billing methods?</h3>
				<p>We accept all the common payment cards including Visa, Mastercard and American Express. The booking needs to be paid in full when a job is confirmed - this is needed in order to ensure models are paid on time. We hold all funds in Escrow until all parties have agreed the work is complete, at which point disbursements (payments to models or refunds to you) are made automatically.</p> 
				
				<h3>How can I view and download my invoices?</h3>
				<p>Go to the invoices section to view the total payments due for all jobs you have created and finalised, along with your booking history. For each booking, you will be able to see a breakdown of the status, date, location, amount, fees & taxes, and other details.</p>


